; Revision 14's paging over slots at 2 M words (contract G3 revision 14, 9.3
; and section 12's Y2 checks; lisp/rev14-paging.lisp).  Run it on a machine of
; 2 M words of main memory (quux --main-memory-size 2MW, through a --quux
; wrapper); at more nothing is forced out and the first case fails.
; the generational collector (contract G3 step 2, Q-GCa) turns automatic
; collection on at boot; its flips, a tenured one after the large arrays below
; above all, touch the pages this check plants (measured on step 2's first
; band: of the 400 fresh pages, the ones out of core had taken slots, 388 of
; them, and 200 read back other than the fresh fill).  Off first, as revision
; 14's band had it.
(progn (when si:gc-on (si:gc-off)) si:gc-on) => NIL
(<= (si:rev14p-memory-words) (* 2 1024 1024)) => T
(si:rev14p-word #o224) => 0
; Fresh pages: 400 pages read, never written, each the fresh fill.
(si:rev14p-fresh-region)
(si:rev14p-fresh-read 16 416) => 0
; The round trip: a 2.5 M-word array filled, read back whole, then forced out
; by 1.5 M-word arrays; the pages that went out have slots, and every element
; comes back.
(si:rev14p-fill 2500000)
(si:rev14p-verify) => 0
(si:rev14p-push 1500000)
(si:rev14p-push 1500000)
(let ((p (si:rev14p-pages si:*rev14p-rt*))) (list (> (first p) 1000) (second p))) => (T 0)
(si:rev14p-verify) => 0
; The fresh pages forced out unwritten took no slot, and read again are the
; fresh fill.
(let ((o (si:rev14p-fresh-out 16 416))) (list (> (first o) 100) (second o))) => (T 0)
(si:rev14p-fresh-read 16 216) => 0
; and pages were written out and read back on the way (A 154 and 155)
(let ((c (si:rev14p-counters))) (list (> (first c) 1000) (> (second c) 1000))) => (T T)
(si:rev14p-word #o224) => 0
; PAGE-IN-WORDS after eviction (the planted test): a young array of 1 M words in
; ephemeral space, filled, forced out by the arrays above, then paged in whole
(si:rev14p-young-fill 1000000) => (T 1000000)
(si:rev14p-push 1500000)
(si:rev14p-push 1500000)
(let ((p (si:rev14p-young-in-core))) (> (second p) 100)) => T
(progn (si:page-in-words (aloc si:*rev14p-young* 0) (array-length si:*rev14p-young*)) (second (si:rev14p-young-in-core))) => 0
(si:rev14p-young-verify) => 0
(si:rev14p-word #o224) => 0
